commit 1b6f47458ace146cb042e4c03a1f7de304c8623d
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Fri Aug 21 16:43:53 2026 +0000

    fix(deps): [perl] package Specio 0.53 as packetfence-perl 1.2.7
    
    1ed07b1916 bumped Specio 0.47 -> 0.53 in dependencies.csv and the version
    was raised in the packetfence-perl spec and in the PacketFence Debian
    dependency, but the rest of the bump was missing.
    
      * The 1.2.7 debian/changelog entry had no blank line after the header and
        no trailer, the same defect 7084238d0b fixed for 1.2.5: dpkg reads into
        the 1.2.6 header where it expects change data or a trailer, and the
        current version ends up with no Date or Maintainer.
    
      * rpm/packetfence.spec still required packetfence-perl >= 1.2.6, so the
        RPM would install against a lib_perl tree holding Specio 0.47.
    
      * The packetfence-perl spec had no %changelog entry for 1.2.7.
    
      * Specio 0.53 ships two new modules, Specio::PP and Specio::XS, the
        Clone::PP and Clone backends it now selects through
        Module::Implementation. Added the matching virtual packages to Provides
        so the list still mirrors what the package installs.
    
    0.53's new runtime prereqs (Clone, Clone::PP, Module::Implementation) are
    already in the tree, so dependencies.csv needs no new rows.
    
    Verified: rpmspec reports 1.2.7-1.el8 and parses the new changelog entry;
    dpkg-parsechangelog reads Version 1.2.7 with its date and maintainer;
    Dpkg::Control::Info parses the 4594 Provides entries. Specio 0.53 passes
    its own suite 348/348 against our lib_perl, with-moose and with-moo
    included, and the DateTime stack that depends on it (DateTime 1.65,
    DateTime::Locale, DateTime::TimeZone, DateTime::Format::Strptime,
    Log::Dispatch) loads and round-trips, constraint-failure path included.

