commit fecbddb4985a858d7e5551cdb70ce41b0d173a2b
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 13:17:19 2026 +0000

    fix(ci): address review on the package build fixes
    
    - Stop exporting CI_COMMIT_TIMESTAMP from github.event.head_commit.timestamp.
      It is unset for workflow_dispatch and schedule, and under make -e an empty
      env var still wins over vars.mk's `?=`, so date -u -d "" silently yields
      midnight-of-today (exit 0, so the || fallback never fires) instead of the
      commit time. Dropping it lets vars.mk derive the value from git, which is
      correct for every event type and identical on push.
    
    - Replace the http://cpan.cpantesters.org fallback with
      https://mirror.csclub.uwaterloo.ca/CPAN. CPAN fetches CHECKSUMS from the
      same mirror as the tarball and check_sigs is off by default, so a plaintext
      entry in urllist is a tampering surface. cpan.cpantesters.org serves a
      self-signed cert on 443, so it cannot simply be switched to HTTPS.
    
    - Fix a "dependencie" typo carried over from the old comment.
    
    Verified in a container built from the edited Dockerfile_debian12: urllist is
    the three HTTPS mirrors in order, and CPAN::Shell->get("URI") still pulls
    URI-5.36.tar.gz with a valid checksum through the fallback.

