commit 4bf791f2d4a5ecc03d79d417385fddcef5558a2b
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Wed Aug 19 19:45:12 2026 +0000

    fix(ci): reclaim the workspace before checkout so a broken runner self-heals
    
    The runners are already in the state the previous commit prevents: both
    build-package and build-package2 hold a half-deleted, root-owned .git under
    _work/packetfence/packetfence, so every branch fails in build_preparation
    before it can check out. Nothing that runs after a job -- the workspace chown,
    the job-completed hook -- can recover that, and the two labels
    (packetfence-perl-package-build, package-build) resolve to those same two
    machines, so both are red.
    
    Give every job that checks out on the host a first step that chowns
    $RUNNER_WORKSPACE back to the runner user. Only root can do it and the runner
    user has no sudo, so borrow root from a container: the runner user is in the
    docker group already, as it must be to run container jobs. It probes with find
    first and skips the container when the workspace is clean, so a healthy runner
    pays for one find and no image pull.
    
    The step is inline in each job rather than a local composite action: those are
    loaded from the workspace, which is not checked out yet.

