M	conf/httpd.conf.d/httpd.webservices.tt.example

commit ec663935287f67ecb968ed12f90aa46bca373aec
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 12 12:53:31 2026 -0400

    fix(fingerbank): restore rate-limited query cache and fix cache hygiene
    
    Restore the $RATE_LIMIT cache around fingerbank queries that was lost in
    the collector-architecture rewrite (the constant survived in
    pf::constants::fingerbank, imported but unused since 35e972e9fe).
    pf::fingerbank::process now caches the _query result in the Redis-backed
    fingerbank CHI namespace for $RATE_LIMIT (60s), keyed on the
    profiling-relevant query parameters (QUERY_PARAMETERS + mac) encoded
    canonically. Back-to-back lookups carrying identical attributes -- RADIUS
    accounting interim updates (pf::radius calls process() on every
    Start/Interim-Update), DHCP renews, portal hits -- share the cached
    result instead of each interrogating the collector, and since the cache
    is shared, the limit applies across all pfqueue/RADIUS/portal processes.
    Volatile collector attributes (counters, last_updated) are excluded from
    the key so it is stable across calls.
    
    Also:
    - Set the mac log context in pf::fingerbank::process: pfqueue resets the
      MDC before each task and nothing in the DHCP->fingerbank chain
      repopulated it, so every fingerbank log line from a queue task read
      [mac:unknown], making correlation painful.
    - Clear the fingerbank CHI cache after a successful update-upstream-db:
      the cached model/combination ids refer to the replaced SQLite file and
      were served stale for up to 24h (the sync_* paths already cleared it,
      the pfcron-driven action did not).
    - Resolve the old TODO in fingerbank::Source::LocalDB: the exact
      (CombinationMatchExact) and fuzzy (CombinationMatch) views shared the
      same cache key prefix, so toggling the API key could serve results
      computed by the other view until the cache expired.
    - Remove dead code in fingerbank::Source::Collector::match: the
      upstream_args/query_args JSON was built and never used (the collector
      builds the interrogate query from its own endpoint data).
    - Fix the _refresh_collector_auth POD: the cached request expires with
      the namespace default (24h), it is not "no expiration".

