commit 4d68fd920531581fe009c99595e46721e4a75272
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 11 14:43:14 2026 -0400

    fix(authentication): only query sources with admin rules on admin login
    
    adminAuthentication was trying every internal source in order until one
    accepted the credentials, even sources that cannot grant an access level
    because they have no administration rules. With a RADIUS or LDAP source
    ordered before the source holding the admin accounts, every admin UI/API
    login triggered a needless request to the remote server.
    
    - Skip sources without at least one administration rule: they can only
      ever yield a NONE access level since the access level is matched on
      the same source that authenticated the user.
    - When a source authenticates the user but no administration rule grants
      an access level, continue with the next source instead of returning
      immediately, so a permissive source ordered first can no longer lock
      out a valid admin defined in a later source.

