M	t/unittest/authentication.t

commit 2fff7544bcab8434dbafd2d764d6c397a7f5a5d6
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 11 13:49:02 2026 -0400

    fix(radius): fail the request when the node can't be read instead of fabricating an unreg node
    
    find_or_create no longer clobbers existing rows when the DB read fails
    (51aff68d3c), but pf::radius caught that error and fell back to
    pf::dal::node->new({mac}), a fresh default object (status=unreg,
    pid=default). Two harms followed during a MySQL outage:
    
    - the role engine saw status=unreg on the fabricated object and answered
      with the registration VLAN, moving a registered device off its role VLAN
    - once the DB recovered mid-request, the CLEANUP $node_obj->save upserted
      the default record over the real row, re-unregistering the node through
      a different path than the one 51aff68d3c closed (and logging NULL
      last_seen errors, since update_last_seen's SELECT NOW() had failed)
    
    On a node read error, authorize and vpn now return RLM_MODULE_FAIL so the
    NAS retries and the device keeps its current access, and radius_filter
    declines with RLM_MODULE_NOOP (matching its unknown-switch precedent)
    rather than evaluating filters against fabricated node data. The
    fabricated-object fallback is gone, so nothing is saved over the real row.

