commit ee42ce8177d672e9ae4bcf63d0caaa05603fd0bf
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 15:52:33 2026 -0400

    Escape user input in LDAP filters to prevent injection (#9119)
    
    Three filter-construction sites interpolated user-controlled input into
    LDAP search filters without escaping:
    
    - LDAPSource::ldap_filter_for_conditions - email-based rule matching
      ($params->{email}) used unescaped across four sub-filters
    - LDAPSource::search_attributes_in_subclass - the authenticated PID
      ($username) used unescaped in the post-auth attribute lookup
    - ADSource::findAtttributeFrom - $from_value (username/SPN) used
      unescaped; reached from the NTLM cache population path
    
    Each value is now escaped once via Net::LDAP::Util::escape_filter_value
    before interpolation, matching the existing safe pattern in _makefilter.
    ADSource gains an explicit import of escape_filter_value since it only
    inherits from LDAPSource.

