commit 6fe8c436177b5d2722da6eebbd13ddfe1196e2a1
Author: Satkunas <3904468+satkunas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 20 11:37:17 2026 -0400

    Fix/switch nas config expire pfconfig (#9134)
    
    * Force pfconfig reload of config::Switch before populating radius_nas
    
    switch_freeradius_populate_nas_config relied on the caller (the
    ConfigStore commit path) having already expired the config::Switch
    pfconfig namespace. When the task is invoked directly, the tied
    cached_hash could be served stale data from the daemon cache.
    
    Explicitly expire config::Switch on the local daemon before tying the
    hash so the NAS table is always built from the latest switch config.
    
    * Add the control directory
    
    * Pass switch config into switch_freeradius_populate_nas_config job
    
    In k8s, pfqueue reads config from N remote pfconfig replicas whose config
    is synced asynchronously from git (the pull_expire handler forks and returns
    immediately). The worker could therefore run before the replicas pulled the
    new switches.conf and rebuild radius_nas from stale config.
    
    The previous in-process pfconfig::manager->new->expire(config::Switch) in the
    worker did not help: on the pfqueue pod it rebuilt the namespace from a
    stale/baked-in switches.conf and wrote that into the shared MySQL L2 cache.
    
    Instead, have the producer (which just wrote switches.conf locally) read the
    authoritative config from its local node and pass it into the job payload, so
    the worker no longer depends on git-sync timing or which replica it reads.
    A fallback read is kept for jobs enqueued without config during upgrades.
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>

