commit b9ba47befdf207a7f97174b8e7bcda52bd371f7d
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 16 17:21:49 2026 -0400

    fix(pfconnector): serve local ntlm_auth_host to remotes, not the cloud ClusterIP
    
    The ntlm-auth-api-env served to a pfconnector-remote carried ntlm_auth_host as
    the cloud pfconnector Service ClusterIP (e.g. 10.128.11.192). resource::domains
    rewrites ntlm_auth_host to pfconnector_service_host for cloud-side radiusd, and
    that value reached the remote env (via a stale/overridden config::Domain). On the
    remote, HOST is used by the on-host readiness monitor (curl HOST:LISTEN/ping) and
    the ntlm-auth-api container — none of which can reach the cloud ClusterIP. The
    monitor never got pong, never wrote the PID, so systemd start-timed-out and
    SIGTERM'd the (healthy) ntlm-auth-api container in a tight restart loop.
    
    The remote's ntlm-auth-api is always a local container reachable at
    containers-gateway.internal, so force that in handleRemoteNtlmAuthAPIEnv
    regardless of the cloud-side value. Makes the remote immune to ntlm_auth_host
    drift.

