commit f477a8c41a01c0226d636a715719d2537f577dc7
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 21:54:42 2026 -0400

    feat(domains): auto-provision connector static tunnels on domain commit
    
    Adding a connector-backed domain generates a new static NTLM-auth tunnel
    (ntlm_auth_port+100) in pfconnector_static_connections, but static tunnels were
    only pushed to the k8s Service + bound at connector handshake — so the domain's
    auth path (e.g. the ntlm/test) didn't work until the connector was manually
    reconnected.
    
    Add a pfconnector-server endpoint that binds a connector's not-yet-bound static
    tunnels on its live tunnel and exposes their ports on the Service, and call it
    from the domains controller after create/update commits.
    
    - server: /api/v1/pfconnector/reprovision-static-connections. Diffs the
      connector's static connections against a per-connector bound-set (recorded at
      handshake), binds only the new remotes via BindDynamicRemotes (tied to the
      connection ctx, so cleaned up on disconnect), one-at-a-time so a stale entry
      can't abort the batch, and adds the new ports to the Service idempotently.
      No active tunnel => no-op (provisioned on next connect).
    - pf::connector->reprovision_static: best-effort call to that endpoint.
    - Domains.pm create()/update(): reprovision the owning connector after commit.
    
    Removes the manual 'restart the connector after adding a domain' step.

