commit 2b6620fc7f271dd2648205b3909153f9c421be43
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 21:37:10 2026 -0400

    fix(pyntlm_auth): make primary-worker election work on Redis < 7.0
    
    primary_worker_register used SET ... NX GET (Redis 6.2+) and EXPIRE ... XX GT
    (Redis 7.0+). Against an older Redis (the cloud redis-cache is 3.2.x) the server
    rejects NX+GET with 'ERR syntax error', so the election failed every 2s, spamming
    the log and leaving is_me unset (so gc_expire_redis_locks never ran and
    async-test lock keys could accumulate). Auth itself was unaffected.
    
    Rewrite with widely-supported primitives: claim via SET NX EX, read the current
    holder with a follow-up GET, and refresh the lease with a plain EXPIRE. Same
    best-effort election semantics; the 5s TTL refreshed every 2s makes the small
    set/get non-atomicity harmless. Works on Redis 2.6.12+.

