commit 302ea1fab20739d888f5b18073c1ab75b5bb131b
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 20:51:12 2026 -0400

    fix(domains): namespace connector domains tenant-wide so config::Domain surfaces them
    
    A connector-backed domain was stored as '[<hostname> <id>]' where hostname()
    is the ephemeral pfperl-api pod name. config::Domain::build_child filters
    sections to those matching the READER's hostname (the pfconfig pod), so the
    two never matched in k8s and config::Domain came back empty -> the pfconnector
    server served zero domains -> the remote's domain.conf had no section and
    ntlm-auth-api refused to start ('section <host> <id> does not exist').
    
    A connector domain isn't owned by one host, and can be served by several
    connectors at once (AD on one side, cache-only ntlm-auth-api on another), so
    connector_id is not a valid namespace either. Give connector domains a stable,
    tenant-wide prefix instead:
    
    - config::Domain::build_child: include use_connector domains regardless of the
      section prefix (they're tenant-wide); classic domains keep the per-host filter.
    - Domains.pm: store connector domains under the stable 'connector' prefix
      (CONNECTOR_HOST_ID) instead of hostname(); id() resolves a bare id against the
      connector prefix then the host prefix; all display/validation strips are now
      prefix-agnostic; create()'s ntlm_auth_port scan keys off the same namespace.
    - ConfigStore::Domain::canDelete: strip any prefix before the realm check.
    
    Classic host-local domains are unchanged.

