commit da5d518248fa998e470631cf7fd33d03fc9d637b
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 16:51:16 2026 -0400

    fix(domains): resolve AD server via connector for connector-backed domains
    
    The ~75s stall before the join was pf::util::dns_resolve() in create()/update()
    querying the domain's dns_servers directly. For a connector-backed domain those
    are the customer's on-prem DNS, unreachable from the cloud, so every query timed
    out (Net::DNS timeout=3 retry=2) before falling back to ad_server. dns_servers
    is a required form field, so it can't just be left blank.
    
    For use_connector domains, resolve the AD server through the connector instead:
    pf::factory::connector->resolve() passes a bare IP through as-is and resolves a
    hostname via pfdns-connector (checking it lands in a connector network). The
    common case (ad_server is the DC IP) now skips DNS entirely. Non-connector
    domains keep the existing direct dns_resolve path.

