commit 562c766aa19d0c712266b8c6b6ac6f7c9030a53a
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 16:45:01 2026 -0400

    fix(domains): dial tunnel-owning pod directly for connector join, not the Service ClusterIP
    
    The previous approach patched the freshly-bound dynreverse port onto the
    pfconnector k8s Service, but kube-proxy does not reliably route a
    just-added port through the ClusterIP: the join POST never reached the
    listener (the reaper fired with aliveConns==0), so it still hung and 599'd.
    
    Instead of routing the join through the Service, dial the exact pfconnector
    instance that owns the tunnel — the address pf::connector already used to
    reach the dynreverse API (from Redis). That pod address is directly
    reachable pod-to-pod, so the connection establishes immediately, keeps the
    proxy's aliveConns>=1 (so the inactivity reaper won't reap it mid-join),
    and needs no Service port at all.
    
    - pf::connector::dynreverse gains a pod_direct opt: override the returned
      host with the API client's host instead of PFCONNECTOR_SERVICE_HOST.
    - Domains.pm connector_join_endpoint passes pod_direct=1.
    - Revert the Go Service-patch code (ensureDynReverseServicePort etc.) and
      the expose_service flag — no longer needed.
    - Static join-remote tunnel removal stays (dynreverse fully replaces it).

