commit e29e54c542bf36b1d9593586b6cb48c86bf11085
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 14 15:41:48 2026 -0400

    fix(pfacct): bound NodeSessionCache with an idle TTL to stop the memory leak
    
    NodeSessionCache was created with cache.NoExpiration and no cleanup interval,
    so its janitor never ran. Entries are only removed on an accounting Stop; a
    missed or dropped Stop (routine under load) left the entry in the map forever,
    which shows up as the steady, restart-only-reset climb in anon memory.
    
    Create the cache with a 12h default expiration and a 15m cleanup interval, and
    refresh the expiration on every access so it acts as an idle timeout: active
    sessions (which touch the cache on each interim) never expire, while sessions
    whose Stop was never seen are reclaimed by the janitor.

