commit e5b64b4e7d0ef5688326edda916602d4b86625c2
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 14 13:26:45 2026 -0400

    perf(stats): rewrite radius_audit_log per-switch/connection metrics as GROUP BY
    
    The 8 RADIUS accept/reject/coa/disconnect metrics per switch_id and
    connection_type used a correlated subquery over an unfiltered outer
    scan (`SELECT DISTINCT r.col, (SELECT COUNT(1) ...) FROM radius_audit_log AS r`).
    The outer query read the entire table history (no WHERE), and the count
    re-ran per row on a column with no index, so on large deployments these
    ran for thousands of seconds stuck in "Sending data".
    
    Rewrite each as a plain GROUP BY filtered on auth_status + created_at.
    This is served entirely by the existing auth_status(auth_status,
    created_at) index, touching only the last 600s of rows. Same
    (label, count) result shape for the telegraf mysql input.

