commit 5ea822af5b4d698c1deaaf906bf14c55e732b140
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 16:05:58 2026 -0400

    fix(pfconnector): strip host_id prefix from domain ids served to remotes
    
    Domains are stored in domain.conf keyed as '<hostname> <id>' (the
    host_id namespace prefix added by the domains controller). config::Domain
    serves that full section name as the map key, so handleRemoteNtlmAuthAPIEnv
    was handing pfconnector-remotes a space-containing id like
    'WIN-SDFCMFQ69C9 inverseINC'.
    
    pfconnector-remote-load.sh re-namespaces each domain under its own
    hostname ('[<local-hostname> <id>]' sections, '<id>.env' files) and
    iterates the keys with an unquoted 'for domain in $domains', so a space
    in the key both word-splits the loop and double-prefixes domain.conf.
    The handler's own test fixtures already assume raw, space-free keys.
    
    Strip the '<host_id> ' prefix in maskDomainSecretsForConnector so remotes
    receive the raw id. Ids are alphanumeric and hostnames contain no spaces,
    so the raw id is the token after the last space; already-raw keys pass
    through unchanged.
    
    This surfaced now that domains can actually be created in cloud (the id
    validation fix); the download payload itself is otherwise unchanged.

