M	go/chisel/server/server_handler.go

commit 892a4fdaa78ba7d4a7e3cc6302bb6d73a9792cb2
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 15:53:39 2026 -0400

    fix(domains): validate raw domain id in update() and form validate()
    
    Follow-up to the create() fix. Two remaining spots still validated the
    host_id-namespaced id ('<hostname> <id>') instead of the raw user id:
    
    - update() feeds mergeUpdate's result to validate_item, and mergeUpdate
      sets id to $self->id (the prefixed value). On long cloud hostnames this
      blew the id field's maxlength=30 just like create() did. Strip the
      host_id prefix before validation so the limit applies to the user id.
    
    - The form's validate() regex was changed in 565fab6458 to require the
      prefixed format (^[chars] [alnum]+$). Now that both controller paths
      validate the raw id, revert it to ^[0-9a-zA-Z]+$ so a plain
      alphanumeric id (e.g. 'inverseINC') passes.
    
    Prefixing remains purely a config-store/storage concern; server-side
    validation now matches the frontend, which only ever sees the raw id.

