commit 7e8cf94d724ed7a87d5d574652afb733047eac31
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 15:02:53 2026 -0400

    fix(domains): validate raw domain id before host_id prefix
    
    In cloud/SaaS mode, create() prefixed the domain id with the host's
    hostname ('<host_id> <id>') before running form validation, so the
    id field's maxlength=30 check ran against the namespaced string. On
    instances with a long pod hostname this left almost no usable id
    budget and rejected valid ids with a spurious 422 (e.g. 'inverseINC'
    reported as 38 characters).
    
    Move the host_id prefixing to after validate_item so the 30-char
    limit applies to the raw, user-supplied id. The stored config-store
    section name is unchanged. This also avoids validating an id that
    contains a space (which violates the id's alphanumeric pattern).

