commit 6f04021a1604440157f957cecb2f414e58d64093
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 7 14:01:52 2026 -0400

    fix(pfconnector): bind DNS tunnels on 0.0.0.0 and make k8s port patching idempotent
    
    The DNS branch of resource::pfconnector_static_connections prepended
    pfdns_connector_service_host as the local bind host, unlike the
    RADIUS/NTLM branches. In k8s that value is the pfconnector Service
    ClusterIP, which the pod cannot bind, so the tunnel proxy failed with
    'bind: cannot assign requested address'. Drop the prefix so DNS tunnels
    bind 0.0.0.0 and let the Service provide the front-end IP.
    
    Also fix the Service port patching in the chisel server: remove-by-index
    ops are now sorted descending and sent together with the adds in a
    single atomic patch, so reconnects no longer fail with k8s 'Duplicate
    value' 422s (removing a lower index first shifted later indexes out of
    range, leaving stale ports that the add then collided with).

M	go/chisel/server/server_handler.go
M	lib/pfconfig/namespaces/resource/pfconnector_static_connections.pm

