commit 833dc55d3e37867260d5f1c5675ea9f50bc93a43
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 6 15:37:28 2026 -0400

    feat(pfconnector): forward fingerbank-collector DHCP to pf::api
    
    Add the pfconnector-server /api/v1/pfconnector/process-dhcp endpoint and the
    pf::api::process_dhcp_event method it relays to, so the fingerbank-collector
    can forward captured DHCP packets to PacketFence (a pfdhcplistener
    replacement).
    
    The collector has no listening interface, so process_dhcp_event synthesizes
    the interface/VLAN context process_dhcpv4 needs: traffic is never inline
    (is_inline_vlan=0, the only reader of interface/interface_ip/interface_vlan),
    and net_type='internal' so is_prod_interface() stays false and DHCP does not
    trigger per-packet post-registration conformity scans. src_mac is validated
    unconditionally like pfdhcplistener. DHCPv6 delegates to process_dhcpv6.
    
    The connector handler resolves the webservices endpoint/credentials from
    pfconfig via a memoized jsonrpc2 client (no per-packet socket round-trip) and
    forwards through a bounded background dispatcher, returning 202 immediately
    rather than blocking the collector; the base64 payload is passed verbatim.
    
    Also guard parse_dhcp_ack's subnet-mask (option 1) deref so an ACK without
    option 1 no longer dies.

