commit 348342d4ed53ccdfe147936c3ad22b0176c765e4
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 3 20:27:06 2026 -0400

    fix(pfacct): AAA client must use webservices.aaa_host, not host
    
    NewAAAClientFromConfig built the AAA JSON-RPC client from aaa_proto and
    the aaa port but paired them with the non-AAA webservices host, so the
    configured aaa_host (PF_WEBSERVICES_AAA_HOST) was dead code. In K8s that
    made pfacct dial the compose default containers-gateway.internal:7070
    instead of the in-cluster httpd-aaa service, producing 10s dial timeouts
    on every radius_accounting notify and silently dropping accounting-driven
    work (e.g. update_iplog_with_accounting).
    
    Use webservices.AAAHost, falling back to webservices.Host when unset so
    bare-metal/compose deployments that only configure host keep working.

