commit 7a65c4bff7eefd19629da41c24c6a22a58be3d82
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 3 16:54:56 2026 -0400

    fix(pfconnector): route RADIUS backends by pool port, not pod-declared port
    
    The radius proxy built its auth/acct backend pools from each pod's
    declared containerPort (getPodPort -> ports[0]), falling back to the
    pool default only when no port was declared. pfacct pods advertise
    containerPort 1812 as metadata while their accounting listener is on
    1813/UDP, so accounting packets were shipped to :1812 and dropped with
    'connection refused'.
    
    Always pair the pod IP with the pool's defaultPort (1812 auth /
    1813 acct); the auth/acct informers are already handed the correct
    port, and backendsForPacket routes by packet code independent of port.
    Drop the now-unused getPodPort helper.

