    feat(pfconnector): route accounting through FreeRADIUS to the cloud
    
    Previously NAS accounting bypassed the remote FreeRADIUS (raw 1813 tunnel),
    so it reached the cloud untagged and signed with the switch secret. Route it
    the same way as auth:
    
    - auth.conf: add a UDP 1813 type=acct listener on virtual_server pf-remote
    - packetfence: add home_server pf.remote.acct (udp 18132 acct tunnel, unified
      secret, no status_check), point pf_acct_pool at it with a degraded failover,
      and have server pf-remote's accounting{} call rest-remote so the cloud-down
      verdict drives Proxy-To-Realm (remote vs degraded) like authorize does
    - realm degraded gains acct_pool=degraded_pool, and pf.degraded accounting now
      returns Accounting-Response OK so the NAS stops retransmitting when the cloud
      is unreachable
    
    pre-proxy{} tags PacketFence-ConnectorID and the home_server signs with the
    unified secret, mirroring auth.

