commit 77546608b29385ddfd87987d6f34352b97a43d1d
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 15:05:55 2026 -0400

    fix(security): replace shell command execution with safe_pf_run (#9094)
    
    * fix(ssl): implement modulus_md5 without shelling out
    
    Replace the openssl_modulus_md5 backtick pipeline
    (echo "$data" | openssl $type -noout -modulus | openssl md5 | awk ...)
    with a pure-Perl implementation that extracts the modulus directly from
    the Crypt::OpenSSL objects and hashes "Modulus=<HEX>\n" via Digest::MD5,
    reproducing the exact bytes OpenSSL hashes. Rename to modulus_md5 since
    it no longer shells out to openssl.
    
    This removes a subprocess built from interpolated data and its
    command-injection risk. Add regression tests locking the output to the
    value the OpenSSL CLI pipeline produces for the test cert/key.
    
    * fix(security): replace shell command execution with safe_pf_run
    
    Convert remaining shell-interpolating command execution to safe_pf_run
    (open3 + argument list, no shell), eliminating shell-injection risk:
    
    - pfcmd_vlan: pfcmd node view now passes args as a list
    - SystemServices: systemctl/status no longer build shell-quoted command
      strings; drop now-unused quoted_system_service_id helper
    - domain: remove unused backtick-based run() wrapper
    
    * fix(security): parse AD config files in pure Perl instead of shelling out
    
    migrate.pl extracted the realm, workgroup, AD server and nameserver by
    shelling out to `grep ... | awk ...` pipelines. Replace them with pure-Perl
    parsing: a small _first_config_value() helper for the krb5/samba "key = value"
    files, and the existing pf::util::dns::get_resolv_dns_servers() helper for the
    nameserver. No shell is invoked, and commented-out lines are correctly skipped.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * fix(security): replace pf_run with safe_pf_run in to-13.1 ntlm-auth upgrade
    
    Use safe_pf_run for the timestamp generation instead of pf_run, in line with
    the rest of the safe_pf_run conversion.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * More pf_safe_run
    
    * fix(safe_pf_run): avoid undrained-stderr deadlock and log spam
    
    - git_storage: merge stderr into stdout for git pull/push so safe_pf_run
      drains the child's progress output instead of leaving stderr undrained,
      which could fill the pipe buffer and hang waitpid.
    - services::manager isAlive: accept exit codes 1-4 from 'systemctl
      is-active' so inactive/failed services on this hot path are not logged
      as command failures (matches print_status).
    - pf-mariadb: merge stderr into stdout for the long-running mysqld_safe
      launch to avoid the same undrained-pipe hang.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * fix(safe_pf_run): drain pipes before waitpid to prevent deadlock
    
    The previous fix (44c4d663a1) addressed deadlock by merging stderr to
    stdout at call sites, but the root cause remained: safe_pf_run called
    waitpid() before draining pipes.
    
    When a child writes >64KB to stdout or any data to stderr, it blocks
    waiting for the parent to read. If the parent calls waitpid() first,
    both processes deadlock.
    
    This caused pfdhcplistener to fail in venom tests:
    - getlocalmac() calls safe_pf_run("/sbin/ifconfig", ...)
    - ifconfig output fills pipe buffer
    - safe_pf_run hangs in waitpid()
    - pfconfig times out loading interfaces::dhcplistener_ints
    - @dhcplistener_ints returns empty
    - pfdhcplistener has no interfaces to monitor → exits immediately
    
    Changes:
    - Move pipe drainage (stdout and stderr) BEFORE waitpid()
    - Drain stderr even when not redirected (was completely undrained)
    - Include stderr in error logs for better debugging (truncated to 500 chars)
    - Add redirect_stderr_to_stdout to getlocalmac's ifconfig call to reduce
      pipe pressure from warnings
    
    This completes the deadlock fix that 44c4d663a1 started.
    
    * fix(safe_pf_run): block SIGCHLD so daemon reapers don't steal exit status
    
    safe_pf_run drains the child's pipes to EOF before calling waitpid, so the
    child has already exited by the time it waits. In daemons that install a
    $SIG{CHLD} reaper doing waitpid(-1, WNOHANG) and discarding the status
    (pfconfig, pfqueue, pfqueue-backend, pffilter, pfdhcplistener), that reaper
    collects the child first and our waitpid returns -1 -- a false failure for a
    command that actually succeeded.
    
    This made pfconfig's pull_expire treat a successful `git pull` as failed
    (retry-with-sleep, then exit before socket_expire), so the local config cache
    was never refreshed and stale config was served. It surfaced in the
    configurator venom suite as 401 on admin login and 504 on configurator changes.
    
    Block SIGCHLD with POSIX::sigprocmask across the open3/waitpid window and
    restore the prior mask (SIG_SETMASK) afterward, so safe_pf_run reliably reaps
    its own child. Add a regression test exercising safe_pf_run under a competing
    SIGCHLD reaper.
    
    * fix(signals): restore prior mask with SIG_SETMASK instead of SIG_UNBLOCK
    
    The runtasks/run_tasks loops in pffilter, pfdhcplistener, and pfqueue
    blocked SIGCHLD then unconditionally unblocked it with SIG_UNBLOCK. That
    clears the block even if an outer scope had SIGCHLD blocked on entry.
    
    Capture the previous mask in the third arg of SIG_BLOCK and restore it
    with SIG_SETMASK so the mask returns to exactly its pre-call state,
    matching the pattern used in safe_pf_run (lib/pf/util.pm).
    
    * fix(signals): unblock SIGCHLD in pffilter/pfdhcplistener children
    
    These children are forked inside the parent's SIGCHLD-blocked runtasks
    window, so they inherit a blocked SIGCHLD. They reset disposition to
    DEFAULT and don't fork grandchildren, so it's currently inert, but the
    inherited block would silently bite any future child code that reaps via
    SIGCHLD. Unblock after fork so the child starts with a clean mask, matching
    the unblock already done in pfqueue's run_task child.
    
    * Don't allow a file that starts with a '-' to be treated as flag
    
    * refactor(services): consolidate systemctl show -p calls into systemctlShowProperty
    
    Make systemctlShowProperty a method (chomping output before splitting and
    accepting an optional options hashref) and route pid, isEnabled,
    _unitFileExists, sub_pid, and tracking's pid through it instead of repeating
    the safe_pf_run -> chomp -> split(/=/) pattern.
    
    * Don't allow a file that starts with a '-' to be treated as flag
    
    * Add error handling for systemctl show
    
    * Improve output of test when they fail
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

