commit d429851278ce787f82854d8b5f8b1afc304f621c
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 12:40:21 2026 -0400

    fix(radiusd): detect connector traffic via %{raw:PacketFence-ConnectorID}
    
    The dynamic_clients fake request runs against an empty VPS list, so the
    connector branch could never see PacketFence-ConnectorID: both the bare
    %{PacketFence-ConnectorID} xlat (errored with "Failed retrieving values")
    and the &PacketFence-ConnectorID existence test from 6203f77123 resolve
    empty. The lookup then fell through to the Packet-Src-IP/NAS-IP range
    query and matched the wrong radius_nas row (local_secret), so the
    unified-signed connector packet failed shared-secret validation and was
    dropped as an unknown client.
    
    Read the VSA straight from the raw MSG_PEEK'd packet bytes with
    %{raw:PacketFence-ConnectorID}, mirroring the MAC/IP lookups. Requires the
    companion rlm_raw vendor-matching fix so the VSA (vendor 29464, attr 40)
    is actually found during the byte walk.

