commit 6203f771239d4ab0f4d0542b8cce69f5dec262a8
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 14:56:24 2026 -0400

    fix(radiusd): harden pfconnector dynamic-client detection
    
    The dynamic_clients vhost resolves connector traffic to the shared
    'pfconnector' radius_nas row (secret = unified_api_system_user.pass) by
    detecting the PacketFence-ConnectorID VSA, before falling back to the
    Packet-Src-IP/NAS-IP range lookup. The detection used a bare
    "%{PacketFence-ConnectorID}" xlat string compare, which can resolve empty
    in the dynamic-client fake request, letting the IP lookup match the
    NAS-IP-Address row (e.g. 10.255.255.2 with its own/local secret) and sign
    with the wrong shared secret.
    
    Use an attribute-existence test (&PacketFence-ConnectorID) instead,
    mirroring the %{raw:...} pattern of the sibling MAC/IP lookups, so the
    connector branch fires reliably and connector traffic uses the unified
    secret.

M	raddb/sites-available/dynamic-clients

commit c1108afe7d66e6ac65560f51508b4ef1321d0c49
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 10:57:26 2026 -0400

    fix(pfconnector): sign proxied RADIUS with unified secret on cloud hop
    
    The cloud pfconnector-server re-signed every proxied packet's
    Message-Authenticator with a per-switch secret from foundSecret()
    (NAS-IP/Calling-Station-Id lookup), falling back to LocalSecret. But the
    cloud FreeRADIUS validates connector traffic against the 'pfconnector' NAS
    client whose secret is unified_api_system_user.pass, and the remote
    FreeRADIUS was configured with that same secret. The mismatched key made
    validation fail (shared-secret error).
    
    Feed the proxy unified_api_system_user.pass as its RADIUS secret (cached at
    tunnel/SSH-connection setup) and sign the Message-Authenticator with it
    unconditionally, since all traffic reaching this proxy is connector
    traffic. The reply path is unchanged: replies tunnel back verbatim and the
    remote validates them with the same unified secret. Drops the now-dead
    foundSecret()/IsIPv4() per-switch path.

