commit 855bc9e564544ddeb887cfa747c856455cef4d1b
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 23 13:56:46 2026 -0400

    fix(connector): honor PFCONNECTOR_SERVICE_HOST for dynreverse host in K8S/SaaS
    
    The connector server's dynreverse API returns a tunnel host (e.g.
    containers-gateway.internal) that does not resolve from a K8S/SaaS pod,
    breaking LDAP sources reached through the connector (e.g. EAP-TLS
    authorization against ActiveDirectory falling through to the guest role).
    
    Prefer $ENV{PFCONNECTOR_SERVICE_HOST} whenever it is defined so the
    connector is reached at its actual service address. Classic PF behavior is
    preserved via the existing containers-gateway.internal fallback.
    
    Also normalize the PF_SAAS check to isenabled() to match every other
    PF_SAAS check in the codebase (was a strict 'ne yes' comparison).

