commit 96c92fa7a777cf846d409f86e22d229539ffa3a2
Author: James Rouzier <jrouzier@inverse.ca>
Date:   Mon Jun 22 15:19:19 2026 +0000

    Fix flaky TestRefresher_FetchOnTunnelUp
    
    The test used the hits counter as a proxy for cache readiness, but hits is
    incremented server-side when the request arrives, racing ahead of the
    client-side fetch->decode->set that actually populates the cache. Observing
    hits>=1 did not guarantee the cache was set, so the cache.get() assertion
    could observe nil (~6% failure rate).
    
    Wait on the cache itself via a new waitForCache helper instead of inferring
    readiness from the hits counter.

M	go/chisel/clientapi/multi_domain_config_test.go

