    direct routing to the pf.degraded virtual server.
    
    * Fater fail-over
    
    * Push freshly learned NT keys to credcache on remote variant
    
    When ntlm-auth-api runs next to pfconnector-remote, forward each NT key
    freshly obtained from the DC to http://100.64.0.1:4242/api/credcache/ so
    the connector can mirror it. Fire-and-forget daemon thread using stdlib
    urllib, gated by CREDCACHE_PUSH_URL env var set only by the remote
    systemd unit; classic PF install is unaffected.
    
    * Mirror chi_cache writes to credcache and serve offline NT keys from it
    
    Every update_cache_entry() now POSTs {key,value,expires_at} to the
    credcache endpoint so bad-password counts, dirty/NDL status and fresh
    keys all replicate, and cached_login() falls back to a GET against
    credcache when MariaDB is unreachable or empty so remote auth keeps
    working while the pfconnector tunnel is down. Renames CREDCACHE_PUSH_URL
    to CREDCACHE_URL since the variable now gates both directions.
    
    * Port packetfence-multi-domain authorize to pfconnector-remote
    
    Adds a cloud endpoint (/api/v1/pfconnector/multi-domain-config) that
    returns ConfigRealm + ConfigOrderedRealm + ConfigDomain as JSON, a
    background-refreshed in-memory cache on the remote, and a localhost
    /api/v1/radius/multi-domain/authorize handler that reproduces the logic
    of raddb/mods-config/perl/packetfence-multi-domain.pm::authorize so
    FreeRADIUS on the remote can set PacketFence-Domain / -NTLM-Auth-Host /
    -NTLM-Auth-Port via rlm_rest without shipping multi_domain_constants.pm
    to the remote.
    
    * Package credcache_push.py in packetfence.spec
    
    Fixes "Installed (but unpackaged) file(s) found" RPM build error after
    the credcache module was added alongside the other pyntlm_auth scripts.
    
    * URL-encode credcache GET path components
    
    Domain identifiers (e.g. "pfconnectorOnboarding InverseINC") and
    usernames can contain spaces and other reserved characters that break
    urlopen with "URL can't contain control characters", so percent-encode
    both segments before assembling the GET URL.
    
    * Drop hostname from NT key cache row identifier
    
    chi_cache rows (and the mirrored credcache POST/GET) are now keyed on
    the bare IDENTIFIER instead of "<hostname> <IDENTIFIER>", so multiple
    ntlm-auth-api instances serving the same AD domain share NT keys and
    bad-password counters. The hostname-prefixed c_domain_identifier is
    kept as-is for domain.conf section lookup (per-host config sections are
    intentional, see addons/upgrade/to-14.0-update-domain-config-section.pl).
    Existing per-host cache rows are orphaned and will expire naturally.
    
    * Changed the ip address to connect
    
    * Changed the api endpoint
    
    * Refresh multi-domain cache on pfconnector tunnel-up
    
    Previously the mdCache only fetched on a 300s ticker; if the tunnel was
    down at startup (or during a flap) the cache stayed empty for up to 300s
    and multiDomainAuthorize returned no attributes to FreeRADIUS. Make the
    refresher poll tunnel.IsActive() every 5s and fetch (a) on every down->up
    transition and (b) on the 300s cadence while up. While the tunnel is
    down it skips fetches entirely, removing noisy failure logs.
    
