    * Always inject PacketFence-ConnectorID VSA on RADIUS-handled remotes
    
    Previously the radius proxy was only constructed when chisel ran inside
    Kubernetes; outside k8s the tunnel forwarded RADIUS packets raw, so the
    PacketFence-ConnectorID VSA was never added. Construct a backend-less
    proxy as a fallback and let ProxyPacket route to the chisel remote's
    hostPort when no backend pool is available, so the VSA is added in all
    deployments.
    
    * add ping endpoint to client and server to test availability
    
    * Inject PacketFence-ConnectorID at the remote radiusd pre-proxy
    
    Move VSA injection out of the chisel radius_proxy and into the
    pfconnector-remote FreeRADIUS pre-proxy. The proxy was parsing the
    inbound packet with the local secret and re-signing with the switch
    secret, which caused the central radiusd to accept the request while
    the switch dropped the response due to authenticator mismatch.
    
    - Revert the cc5c6cccfa fallback so non-k8s tunnels forward RADIUS raw
      again; the chisel radius proxy is only constructed for Kubernetes
      deployments where it owns backend-pool routing.
