      not end up with a duplicate attribute.
    
    * Substitute %connector_id% in the container's configure-raddb.sh
    
    The previous commit only updated the host-side copy of configure-raddb.sh
    (installed to /usr/local/pfconnector-remote/bin/), but at service start
    the pfconnector-remote-combined image runs its own copy as an s6 oneshot,
    so %connector_id% was never replaced and the pre-proxy injection was a
    no-op. Mirror the substitution in the container script, sourcing
    connector_id from $AUTH (passed via --env-file by the combined wrapper)
    with a fallback to the bind-mounted pfconnector-client.env file.
    
    * Mirror nt_key cache rows to the radius-receiving connector
    
    When a switch reaches one pfconnector-remote (A) but the AD domain is
    hosted on another (B), B's ntlm-auth-api would only push the nt_key into
    its own connector-cache, leaving A to pay a tunnel round-trip on every
    repeat MS-CHAP. Carry the originating connector_id through the auth path
    and have B mirror the cache write back to A.
    
