    * Fix "Not a HASH reference" in connector status endpoint
    
    readAll('id') returns an array ref, not a hash ref. Use readAllIds()
    instead and iterate with @$connectors rather than %$connectors.
    
    * Fix grey connector status icons - slot scope access was wrong
    
    The cell(status) slot used `item.status` but in BootstrapVue's slot
    scope, the row data is at `item.item`. Since `item.status` on the
    scope wrapper is always undefined, no color class was applied and
    icons rendered as grey/default regardless of the actual status.
    
    * Fix connector status icons not updating reactively
    
    Switched from reactive({}) to ref({}) so the entire status map is
    replaced on each poll. Property-level mutations on reactive objects
    with dynamic keys don't reliably trigger Vue 2 computed re-evaluation,
    causing icons to stay stale until a page refresh.
    
    * Add admin configuration section to pfconnector documentation
    
    Document the three-tab connector configuration workflow: creating
    connectors with network ranges, mapping DNS domain names to connectors
    for FQDN-based routing, and configuring DNS forwarders through the
    connector tunnel. Includes worked examples for Active Directory behind
    a pfconnector.
    
    * Remove obsolete pfconnector systemd units and dead code
    
    Delete unused pfconnector-remote.service (replaced by -combined variant),
    radiusd-auth.service (runs from conf/systemd/), and logrotate-drop-in.
    Update PartOf references and Go chisel API to use the -combined service name.
    Clean up commented-out CONNECTOR_ID extraction from load script.
    
    * Remove unused RPC credentials and dead docker wrappers
    
    Drop rpc_user/rpc_pass from pfconnector radiusd.conf (RPC only needed for
    httpd.aaa, which isn't used in pfconnector-remote-combined). Delete obsolete
    docker wrapper scripts replaced by the combined variant.
    
    * Document NTLM auth services required behind a pfconnector
    
    Explain that when a domain controller is behind a pfconnector, the
    packetfence-ntlm-auth-api-remote and packetfence-ntlm-auth-join-remote
    packages must be installed on the pfconnector-remote host for NTLM SSO.
    
    * Clarify NT Key cache and per-connector NTLM service requirements
    
    Explain that packetfence-ntlm-auth-api-remote is also needed for NT Key
    cache with EAP-PEAP, and must be installed on every pfconnector-remote host
    serving domains with NTLM or NT Key cache.
    
    * Fix NT Key cache scope: only needed for EAP-PEAP, not NTLM SSO
    
    The ntlm-auth-api-remote service is required for NT Key cache on domains
    behind a pfconnector, not for captive portal NTLM single sign-on.
    
    * Clarify that remote NT Key cache provides offline auth resilience
    
    Explain that the local cache keeps authentication working when the domain
    controller or the main PacketFence server is unreachable.
    
    * Remove unused /logs WebSocket handler
    
    The WebSocket log streaming endpoint and its Broadcaster infrastructure
    are not currently used and have been removed.
    
