commit 7e853bd6c2d2c66a36a4de11fcbec8a863565e3c
Author: Durand <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 08:52:06 2026 -0400

    Fix non-deterministic radius filter merge with reply: prefix (#9063)
    
    A filter answer such as 'reply:Cisco-AVPair = ...' was stored under a
    different hash key than the bare 'Cisco-AVPair' set by
    returnRadiusAccessAccept, so handleAnswerInRule never merged them.
    Both keys then crossed the rlm_rest boundary as duplicates targeting
    the same RADIUS attribute, producing a non-deterministic Access-Accept:
    the filter answer randomly disappeared (or displaced an existing
    Cisco-AVPair slot) depending on hash iteration order.
    
    Normalize the leading 'reply:' prefix and combine values into a single
    arrayref. Other section prefixes (control:, request:, session-state:)
    are left untouched so they don't collide with reply attributes.

M	lib/pf/access_filter/radius.pm
M	t/unittest/access_filter/radius.t

commit f67f696e14a4acd7744fcbfa9785bbcffaf5bfc7
Author: Durand <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 08:50:51 2026 -0400

    Fixes a pfcmd configreload hang and the slow switch-config admin UI, both rooted in unbounded per-role switch mappings, plus a UX improvement for blocked role deletions. (#9078)
    
    * fix(pfconfig): dedup resource expiry to stop configreload hang
    
    expire_all/expire recursively hard-expired every child_resource of every
    namespace with no de-duplication. Shared children (e.g. resource::RolesReverseLookup
    is a child of 13 namespaces) were rebuilt once per parent, so on a large config
    'pfcmd configreload hard' issued 1000+ redundant rebuilds and effectively never
    returned.
    
    Thread a per-run %seen set through expire_all/expire so each namespace is
    rebuilt at most once per run (config is static during a run, so this is
    idempotent). The optional $seen param keeps all other callers backward
    compatible.
    
    * fix(roles): clean switch role mappings on delete and show referencing ids
    
    Deleting a role never pruned its per-role keys (<role>Vlan, <role>Url, ...)
    from switches, so over create/delete cycles switches.conf accumulated thousands
    of orphaned mappings, bloating the switch-config API (a single switch GET was
    ~1MB / ~19s).
    
    - Add prune_role_from_switches() (factored out of the rename/reassign path) and
      a post_remove() hook so deleting a role removes its mappings from all switches.
    - When a delete is blocked because the role is still in use, include the
      referencing ids in the 422 error (new 'ids' field + ids appended to the
      message), so users see exactly which switches/entities still use the role.
    - Admin UI reassign dialog now lists those ids per category instead of the raw
      reason code.
    - Add tools/prune_orphaned_switch_role_mappings.pl to clean pre-existing orphans
      (dry-run by default, --commit to apply; protects roles.conf + built-in roles).
    
    * fix(roles): migrate switch role mappings on reassign instead of dropping them
    
    reassign_role_config_store_switch only pruned the old role's per-role
    switch mapping keys (${old}Role, ${old}Vlan, ...) without moving them
    to the new role, so reassigning old -> new silently lost all
    switch-specific Role/Vlan/Url/... mappings.
    
    Add migrate_role_in_switches() to rename those keys to the new role
    (preserving any mapping the new role already had), and keep
    prune_role_from_switches for the delete path.

