commit 6795a89fd087fb65da62b71d6b963060db406805
Author: Durand <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 08:45:18 2026 -0400

    fingerbank: refresh collector auth header at request time (#9105)
    
    The collector request built by fingerbank::Collector::build_request bakes
    the 'Authorization: Token <api_key>' header into the HTTP::Request, and
    pf::fingerbank caches that request object in the Redis-backed 'fingerbank'
    CHI namespace with no expiration (keyed per-MAC). When the Fingerbank API
    key is rotated, the cached request keeps sending the old token, so the
    collector returns 401 Unauthorized until the cache is manually flushed --
    a service restart does not help because the cache is persistent.
    
    Set the Authorization header from the current config on each request
    instead of relying on the cached value. fingerbank::Config reloads
    fingerbank.conf on file mtime change, so this picks up key rotations
    immediately with no cache flush required.
    
    Affects endpoint_attributes() and update_collector_endpoint_data().

M	lib/pf/fingerbank.pm

commit 77ad59aaa8767314f71d6f3b3140012425c4ac88
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 11:28:47 2026 -0400

    DHCP processor: fix firewallsso refresh gate and fingerbank DHCPv6 signature
    
    Two correctness fixes in the per-packet suppression logic:
    
    - firewallsso: on IP change the code removed the half-lease refresh key
      for the new IP, which made the Update block below see a miss and fire a
      redundant Update on the same packet (Start had already established the
      session). Set the key instead so this packet — and renewals within the
      half-lease — skip the Update, matching the comment's intent.
    
    - fingerbank: the suppression signature only hashed dhcp_fingerprint,
      dhcp_vendor and computername, but the processor also maps and records
      dhcp6_fingerprint and dhcp6_enterprise. A change in only the DHCPv6
      fields was wrongly suppressed; include them in the signature.

