commit ce310f2b20aebaf4ac128e708d355a43b6716844
Author: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 10 16:52:26 2026 +0000

      perf(pfappserver): coalesce node_category lookups into batched search
    
      The node table's category_id/bypass_role_id formatters resolved each
      row's role name individually. When the full roles list wasn't already
      cached, every row dispatched its own GET /node_category/<id>, producing
      an N+1 request storm (thousands of identical calls on large tables).
    
      Make role-name resolution lazy and coalesced:
      - Add a reusable createBatchLoader util (DataLoader pattern): in-flight
        dedup, windowed batching, and an optional result/negative cache.
      - Resolve category ids via a batched POST node_categories/search (an
        `or` of `equals`, since the search API has no `in` operator) instead
        of one GET per id.
      - Cache per-id results in a reactive `cachedRoles` array (separate from
        the full `roles` list) so table cells re-render as names arrive.
      - Drop the eager getRoles() bulk-load from the formatters; only the
        visible page's distinct roles are fetched on demand.
    
      A typical page now resolves all role names in a single request; large
      pages collapse thousands of lookups into a handful of batched calls.

