commit 7ff3989480cd623eff2a3553359a546fdc8ab81d
Author: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 20:40:25 2026 +0000

    refactor(db): decorate via DBI RootClass subclass to cover static SQL
    
    The Callbacks/@_-rewrite approach could only modify a writable lexical: any
    static string literal passed to prepare/prepare_cached/do is read-only, so the
    interim "skip read-only args" fix silently left ALL static SQL undecorated.
    
    Switch to subclassing the DBI handle via the RootClass connect attribute. The
    pf::db::dbi::db overrides for prepare/prepare_cached/do receive the statement as
    a normal parameter, build a fresh decorated copy with _decorate_statement, and
    hand it to SUPER:: -- no @_ aliasing, so static literals and lexicals are both
    decorated. The select* helpers call prepare internally and are covered
    transitively. set_session and the connected callback are unchanged.
    
    Verified against live MariaDB: db_connect() succeeds (handle is pf::db::dbi::db),
    a static $dbh->prepare("SELECT 1") and selectrow_arrayref are decorated, the DAL
    db_execute path returns 200 with a decorated statement, and pfcmd checkup shows
    no database errors.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

