commit 9575e27c8a637429b32566f988c17cbba8273c12
Author: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 19:28:28 2026 +0000

    fix(db): assign decorated SQL in place and skip read-only literals
    
    The DBI callback rewrote the statement by modifying @_, but two problems
    surfaced at runtime:
    
      - Read-only literals (e.g. set_session's $dbh->do("SET SESSION ...")) cannot
        be assigned through the @_ alias and died with "Modification of a read-only
        value attempted", breaking db_connect and the config sanity check.
      - splice(@_, ...) avoids the error but DBI does not see the replacement, so
        the comment would never reach the wire.
    
    DBI only honors an in-place $_[N] assignment. The DAL (db_execute) and the
    legacy db_query_execute framework both pass a writable lexical, so those -- the
    routable application queries -- are decorated and propagate correctly. Wrap the
    assignment in eval and skip on read-only: connection-setup literals like
    SET SESSION are not routed queries and are fine left undecorated.
    
    Verified end to end against the live DB: db_connect() succeeds and a
    prepare_cached query emits /* pf:<service> */ SELECT ... .
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

