    fix(venom): sanitize all log dirs and prevent unsanitized archive creation
    
    Fixes intermittent failures on pfdeb12dev where script would exit on errors
    while node01 succeeded (no Psono vars present). Script now ensures secrets
    never leak in archived logs.
    
    Changes:
    - Remove errexit to allow proper error handling without killing script early
    - Track sanitization failures and refuse archive creation if any occur
    - Sanitize /var/log and /usr/local/pf/logs in addition to venom results
    - Check both PSONO_CI_API_KEY_ID and PSONO_CI_API_SECRET_KEY_HEX before attempting secret fetches
    - Handle tar exit code 1 (file changed warnings) as non-fatal
    - Suppress psonoci error output to prevent secret fragment leakage
    - Add clear ERROR/FATAL/SUCCESS messages for debugging
    
    Security: If ANY secret cannot be fetched or sanitized, script exits with
    code 1 and no archive is created, preventing exposure of secrets.

