commit 26c1e7b74c719324b2a0045940390ae0298b2cc8
Author: JeGoi <13801368+JeGoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 1 14:33:50 2026 -0400

    fix(ci): set deploy-dir and friendly-name vars in .deploy_pkg_rules
    
    The deploy_packages matrix job traverses only .deploy_pkg_rules, which set
    DEPLOY_ENV_NAME/IMAGE_TAG but not DEB_DEPLOY_DIR/RPM_DEPLOY_DIR nor the
    *_DEST_NAME friendly names. Those lived solely in .context_rules, which
    deploy_packages does not reference, so deploy-artifacts.sh fell back to its
    defaults: DEB_DEPLOY_DIR=:-foo published packages under
    PacketFence/foo/<version>/ instead of debian/, and feature-branch builds
    emitted versioned production filenames (e.g. packetfence-export_15.2.deb)
    into the shared debian/ and RHEL* dirs, overwriting release artifacts.
    
    Mirror the per-context values from the pre-matrix maintenance branches into
    .deploy_pkg_rules: debian / debian-branches for the deb dir, branches/x86_64
    for the branch rpm dir, and the *-branches / _devel friendly names. Feature
    branches now publish packetfence-export_branches.deb etc.; only devel,
    maintenance, and release emit the versioned names.

