commit ffdaf5ec82f2295e88e39d2f3db9f7608d600eea
Author: JeGoi <13801368+JeGoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 1 09:57:54 2026 -0400

    ci: consolidate GitLab pipeline into parameterized DAG and containerize build/sign/deploy (#9050)
    
    * refactor(ci): consolidate GitLab pipeline into parameterized DAG
    
    Collapse the four per-context (devel/maintenance/branches/release) job copies
    into single jobs driven by .context_rules as the single source of truth for
    $CONTEXT and $IMAGE_TAG, composed with reusable feature-gate rule fragments
    via !reference. Merge build_img and build_img_container into one build_images
    stage ordered by needs:, drop ~30 _branches test duplicates and per-context
    image trims, and add the TEST_ONLY variable for selective test execution.
    
    * build(ci): replace Packer/Ansible build with Docker pfbuild images
    
    Remove the Packer + Ansible pfbuild/cpanbuild provisioning trees and build the
    pfbuild base images from Dockerfiles (pfbuild-centos-8, pfbuild-bookworm)
    consumed via Kaniko. Drop gitlab-buildpkg-tools: build_rpm/build_deb now call
    rpmbuild/debuild directly with CI version suffixes derived in config.mk, and
    get_pf_release() no longer depends on perl. Pass GOVERSION/PF_MINOR_RELEASE to
    the pfbuild Dockerfiles via kaniko_vars.
    
    * refactor(ci): run signing, publishing and deploy in containers
    
    Add signing-packages and publish-ppa container images and move sign_packages,
    publish_ppa and deploy_* onto the docker executor. Replace the PPA tooling with
    generate-pages.sh (real APT/YUM repo metadata + index pages) and
    update-changes-checksums.py (regenerate .changes checksums after dpkg-sig).
    deploy-artifacts.sh honours an ssh_deploy_config; publish-to-git.sh relies on
    gh preinstalled in the image; exclude CI-only images from the on-prem pull.
    
    * build(ci): move material generation into pfconfig wrapper image
    
    Add a CI-only pfconfig-material-builder image (gh + python3-nacl + git) so the
    customer-facing pfconfig image stays slim, and run generate-material.sh inside it.
    
    * ci(github): update reusable workflows and drop debian11
    
    Align the reusable GitHub Actions workflows (sign_packages, unit_test,
    upload_packages) and their callers with the consolidated pipeline, and remove
    debian11 from the build/test matrices.
    
    * test(venom): add unit_tests_deb12 target
    
    Add Debian 12 parity for the unit_tests Venom scenario.
    
    * fix(ci): gate build_artifacts_material by build_img_container
    
    build_artifacts_material runs in the pfconfig-material-builder image, which is
    built by the pfconfig_material_builder job (gated by .gated_by_build_img_container).
    The material job lacked that gate, so BUILD_ARTIFACTS_MATERIAL=yes with
    BUILD_IMG_CONTAINER=no would schedule it with no image to pull (its needs: on the
    wrapper job is optional). Add the same gate so the two jobs activate together.
    
    * fix(signing-packages): verify dpkg-sig .deb checksum before install
    
    The dpkg-sig .deb is fetched over HTTPS from archive.debian.org and installed
    without integrity verification, relying solely on TLS. Pin the SHA256 (verified
    against the signed bullseye main Packages index) and check it with sha256sum -c
    before apt-get install to guard against archive tampering / MITM.

