commit 529b49fb02df54195d9c3b8d18a0b0da288d1ea0
Author: Durand <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu May 28 11:52:22 2026 -0400

    Feature/voip dacl (#9068)
    
    * Add VoIPDACL switch toggle: merge full Access-Accept with Voice VSA
    
    When VoIPDACL is enabled on a switch (or switch group), pf::radius::authorize
    keeps the Voice VSA returned by _authorizeVoip but no longer shortcuts to
    CLEANUP. The phone falls through to fetchRoleForNode + returnRadiusAccessAccept
    so the regular reply (VLAN tunnel attributes, role attributes, push/downloadable
    ACLs, access-filter rules) is computed as if the device were a non-VoIP
    endpoint. The captured Voice VSA is then merged on top via a new helper
    _merge_radius_attrs that promotes duplicate keys (e.g. Cisco-AVPair) to
    arrayrefs so multivalued attributes are preserved.
    
    When VoIPDACL is on, the VoIP-only synchronize_locationlog write in
    _authorizeVoip is skipped; the main flow's write happens with the computed
    role/vlan instead.
    
    Default: N. Wired into the Perl form, both Vue forms (switches and
    switchGroups), the Go pfconfigdriver struct and switches.conf.defaults.
    
    Tests: t/unittest/radius_voip_dacl.t exercises _merge_radius_attrs across
    disjoint, duplicate, arrayref, mixed, empty and falsy-value inputs, plus
    the new _VoIPDACL switch field default and parsing via two new fixtures
    in t/data/switches.conf.
    
    * Render VoIPDACL toggle in switch admin UI and document in OpenAPI
    
    The previous VoIPDACL commit added the <form-group-voip-dacl> tag to
    the switch and switch-group edit templates and re-exported
    FormGroupVoipDacl from each _components/index.js, but TheForm.vue
    never imported or locally registered the component — so the toggle
    silently rendered as nothing. Add it to both the import destructure
    and the components object in switches/ and switchGroups/, and add
    VoIPDACL to the four matching entries in docs/api/spec/openapi.yaml
    for documentation parity.
    
    * Rename VoIPDACL toggle to VoIPFullAuthorization
    
    The toggle was named VoIPDACL / "Send ACLs for VoIP", but it does far
    more than send ACLs: when enabled it runs the phone through the regular
    authorize flow and merges the FULL Access-Accept (VLAN tunnel attributes,
    role attributes, push/downloadable ACLs, access-filter rules) on top of
    the Voice VSA. The name undersold the behavior -- the VLAN-conflict caveat
    in the help text only exists because it sends VLAN/tunnel attributes too.
    
    Rename the config key, internal switch key, form field/label, Vue
    components, Go struct, OpenAPI spec, and tests/fixtures to
    VoIPFullAuthorization / "Full RADIUS authorization for VoIP". Behavior is
    unchanged.
    
    NOTE: this renames a config key. Anyone who set VoIPDACL=Y on this branch
    will fall back to the default (off) until they set VoIPFullAuthorization=Y.
    No released-config impact since the feature is unreleased.

