commit 9d2a7eb35d68b55fd794fda22c406b6940dcddbb
Author: JeGoi <13801368+JeGoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue May 26 16:15:17 2026 -0400

    feat(ci): bump VirtualSwitch to 2.6.31 in venom tests and allow TEST_ONLY to trigger CI (#9032)
    
    * Bump virtualswitch package version to 2.6.12-1
    
    * Align venom virtualswitch config deploy with virtualswitch 2.6.12
    
    Drop coa_enabled/coa_port from the radius YAML block: virtualswitch
    2.6.12 has no such fields, CoA is configured via the systemd unit's
    -enable-coa/-coa-addr CLI flags.
    
    Bump default ipfix_destination_port from 2055 to 4739 to match the
    IANA-registered default introduced in virtualswitch 2.6.11.
    
    * Allow TEST_ONLY to trigger CI tests and accept comma-separated patterns
    
    TEST_ONLY now triggers test jobs on its own (no need to also set
    TEST=yes) and accepts a comma-separated list (e.g. auth,virtual) which
    is translated internally to regex alternation.
    
    * Allow TEST_ONLY to trigger PPA publish so test VMs can fetch packages
    
    Tests fetch packages from the per-pipeline PPA URL
    (http://inverse.ca/downloads/PacketFence/gitlab/${CI_PIPELINE_ID}),
    so the publish_ppa job must run whenever tests run. Without this,
    TEST_ONLY-triggered pipelines schedule the test stage but no PPA is
    published, leaving test VMs without packages.
    
    * Bump virtualswitch package version to 2.6.31-1
    
    * Fix TEST_ONLY pattern security and correctness issues
    
    Address two issues in TEST_ONLY comma-to-regex translation:
    
    1. Empty alternation: Filter out empty/whitespace items to prevent patterns
       like "mac_auth," from becoming "mac_auth|" which matches empty string
       (and thus every job name unintentionally).
    
    2. Option injection: Add "--" before grep pattern to prevent TEST_ONLY
       values starting with "-" from being interpreted as grep options.
    
    * Add guard against empty TEST_ONLY pattern
    
    Prevent TEST_ONLY values containing only commas/whitespace (e.g., ",,," or "   ")
    from producing an empty regex pattern. An empty pattern would match every job name,
    causing all tests to run unintentionally. Now exits with error if no valid test
    names remain after filtering.

