commit 1024d3b85560e538a9d82aaafe54e9d1c78a0a32
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue May 5 08:17:08 2026 -0400

    Roles form: don't let Select re-default parent_id over explicit null
    
    cleanupItemForCreate already normalizes JSON `parent_id: null` to '' in
    the controller, but `HTML::FormHandler::Field::Select::_result_from_input`
    re-applies `$self->default` whenever the result has no value. Empty-string
    input on a Select coerces to undef, so the form clobbered the empty back
    to `advanced.default_role_parent_id` before the value reached the config
    store, persisting `parent_id=<default>` instead of the explicit empty
    lock the user asked for.
    
    Short-circuit `default_parent_id` to undef whenever the form is being
    processed with `parent_id` in params. The OPTIONS path (no params) still
    returns the default, so the new-role UI dropdown pre-selects
    `advanced.default_role_parent_id` as before.

