commit 5ca02b5ad91419afa9ef782f6691a26930427766
Author: Durand <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Apr 30 17:03:37 2026 -0400

    Roles: fix parent_id semantics across create, update, and admin UI (#9029)
    
    * Roles: fix parent_id semantics across create, update, and admin UI
    
    - UnifiedApi/Controller/Config/Roles: distinguish payload-omitted vs
      explicit-null parent_id on the raw JSON before the form coerces both
      to undef. cleanupItemForCreate seeds advanced.default_role_parent_id
      only when the key is missing; cleanupItemForUpdate locks parent_id=
      on explicit null. Also strip parent_id out of standardPlaceholder so
      the default_role_parent_id name no longer leaks into the parent_id
      field placeholder for new roles.
    - Form/Config/Roles::default_parent_id: only fire the default for
      brand-new roles ($no_id). Existing roles must respect their stored
      value, otherwise cleanup_item's posted=>0 processing reasserts the
      default in API reads and the parent_id dropdown reappears with the
      default after the admin clears it.
    - ConfigStore/Roles::cleanupBeforeCommit: shrink to a defensive backstop
      (undef on create -> ''). The controller now owns the default lookup.
    - pfconfig/namespaces/config/Roles: at build_child time, materialize
      advanced.default_role_parent_id only when the parent_id key is fully
      absent in roles.conf (e.g. roles predating the create-time fix), so
      the RADIUS/Switch.pm parent walks fire. parent_id= (explicit empty)
      stays empty -- the lock is preserved.
    - pfconfig/namespaces/config/Pf: declare config::Roles as a child so
      pf.conf changes invalidate %ConfigRoles.
    - TheForm.vue (admin UI): when the user explicitly clears parent_id,
      reset the inherited acls/max_nodes_per_pid placeholders to empty
      rather than falling back to the default_role_parent_id values.
    - UnifiedApi/Controller/Config::ensure_integer_fields: gate int() on
      looks_like_number so Template Toolkit expressions and empty strings
      (e.g. fingerbank_settings host/port) are not silently coerced to 0
      with a "isn't numeric" warning.
    
    * Roles: apply parent_id null/missing normalization to PUT replace too
    
    cleanupItemForUpdate only fires on PATCH; the base controller's replace
    (PUT) bypassed all the raw-payload normalization, so {"parent_id": null}
    on PUT was passed through as undef and ended up removing the param from
    storage instead of writing the explicit empty lock that PATCH produces.
    
    Add a cleanupItemForReplace hook in the base Config controller (default
    pass-through, called between get_json and validate_item) and override it
    in the Roles controller to delegate to cleanupItemForCreate, since PUT's
    replace-the-whole-thing semantics line up with the create-side matrix
    (missing -> default_role_parent_id, null -> '' lock, value -> as-is).
    
    * ConfigStore::Roles: refresh cleanupBeforeCommit POD
    
    The previous POD still described the old behavior where this method
    materialized parent_id from advanced.default_role_parent_id on CREATE.
    That logic moved to the UnifiedApi Roles controller hooks
    (cleanupItemForCreate / cleanupItemForReplace / cleanupItemForUpdate),
    with a runtime fallback for legacy roles in pfconfig's build_child.
    Update the POD to describe what cleanupBeforeCommit actually does now
    (defensive backstop: undef-on-create -> '') and point at where the
    real default-parent resolution lives.
    
    * Roles: cover parent_id missing/null/empty matrix in unit tests
    
    Add assertions in t/unittest/UnifiedApi/Controller/Config/Roles.t that
    read parent_id straight off cachedConfig after each write, so we lock
    in the create/update behavior:
    
      CREATE  omitted     -> advanced.default_role_parent_id (r4 in fixture)
      CREATE  null        -> '' (empty lock)
      CREATE  ''          -> '' (empty lock)
      CREATE  '<value>'   -> '<value>'
      UPDATE  omitted     -> preserved (mergeUpdate)
      UPDATE  null        -> '' (empty lock)
      UPDATE  ''          -> '' (empty lock)
      UPDATE  '<value>'   -> '<value>'
    
    Also extend cleanupItemForUpdate so an explicit empty string is treated
    the same as null (both = "user cleared the field"). Previously only
    null was normalized; '' fell through the form-coercion to undef and
    landed in storage as a removed param on UPDATE because the
    cleanupBeforeCommit backstop only fires on CREATE.
    
    * fix UI role inheritance
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>

