    USB bootable ISO: self-contained PacketFence installer for Debian 12 (#9027)
    
    * Add Makefile for USB bootable ISO build
    
    Adds the main entry point Makefile for building the offline
    USB bootable ISO. Provides iso, clean, and upload targets.
    
    * Add build-and-upload.sh for USB bootable ISO
    
    Script handles building the USB ISO and uploading to Linode S3.
    Upload directory uses version with -usb suffix (e.g., v15.0.0-usb).
    Supports any branch name with automatic slash-to-dash conversion.
    
    * Add build-usb-bootable-iso.sh main build script
    
    Main script that orchestrates the USB bootable ISO build process:
    - Downloads base Debian ISO
    - Creates local APT repository
    - Pre-downloads Docker images
    - Injects preseed configuration
    - Builds hybrid ISO for UEFI and Legacy BIOS boot
    
    * Add create-local-repo.sh for offline APT repository
    
    Creates a local APT repository containing all packages needed
    for offline PacketFence installation:
    - Base Debian packages
    - PacketFence and dependencies (MariaDB, Redis, Docker, FreeRADIUS)
    - Generates Packages index and Release file
    
    * Add predownload-docker-images.sh for offline Docker images
    
    Downloads all PacketFence Docker images from ghcr.io registry
    and saves them as tar.gz files for offline installation.
    Includes a loader script to import images on target system.
    
    * Add preseed-offline.cfg.tmpl for offline installation
    
    Debian preseed configuration for offline USB installation:
    - Disables network mirror usage
    - Uses local repository from ISO
    - Runs post-installation script for PacketFence setup
    - Supports both UEFI and Legacy BIOS
    
    * Add postinst-offline.sh for offline post-installation
    
    Post-installation script for offline USB installation:
    - Configures local APT repository from ISO
    - Installs PacketFence from local packages
    - Loads pre-downloaded Docker images
    - Resets MariaDB root password
    - Creates first-boot service for final configuration
    
    * Add boot configuration files for USB offline installer
    
    GRUB and ISOLINUX boot menu configurations:
    - grub.cfg: UEFI boot menu
    - menu.cfg: BIOS boot menu structure
    - gtk.cfg: Graphical boot entry
    - drkgtk.cfg: Dark contrast accessibility option
    
    * Add .gitignore for USB bootable ISO build directory
    
    Ignores generated files, work directories, downloaded ISOs,
    local APT repository, and Docker images cache.
    
    * Add USB bootable ISO job to GitLab CI
    
    Adds CI job for building USB bootable offline installer ISO:
    - New variable USB_ISODIR pointing to ci/usb-bootable-iso
    - Rule .build_pf_img_usb_iso_any_branch_rules for any branch
    - Job template .build_pf_img_usb_iso_job
    - Job build_pf_img_usb_iso triggered by BUILD_PF_IMG_USB_ISO=yes
    
    Upload directory uses branch name with -usb suffix.
    
    * Fix maintenance branch version format in USB ISO upload
    
    Convert maintenance/15.0 to v15.0.0 format to match the
    regular ISO upload directory naming convention.
    
    * Fix clean target permission error in USB ISO Makefile
    
    Add chmod +w before rm to handle read-only files extracted
    from the Debian ISO during build process.
    
    * Fix permission error when copying menu.cfg in USB ISO build
    
    Add menu.cfg to chmod command before copying boot configuration
    files. The file extracted from Debian ISO is read-only.
    
    * Reduce wget output noise for base ISO download
    
    Remove --show-progress flag to avoid verbose progress output
    in CI logs. Only show download start and completion messages.
    
    * Fix ISO volume ID exceeding 32 character limit
    
    Extract branch name after "/" (e.g., feature/foo -> foo) and
    truncate to 26 chars to fit "PFusb-" prefix within ISO 9660 limit.
    Added debug output showing volume ID construction.
    
    * Fix ISO build errors: symlink loops and oversized repo
    
    - Remove -follow flag from find to avoid filesystem loops with symlinks
    - Don't copy packages from host /var/cache/apt/archives (caused 30GB bloat)
    - Shorten volume ID to 16 chars max for Joliet compatibility (PF-xxx format)
    
    * Save all Docker images in single archive to deduplicate layers
    
    Instead of saving each image separately (duplicating shared base layers),
    save all images with a single 'docker save' command. This allows Docker
    to deduplicate common layers, significantly reducing the archive size.
    
    * Use debootstrap chroot for complete offline package download
    
    Replace unreliable apt-get download approach with a proper chroot-based
    method using debootstrap. This ensures ALL dependencies are correctly
    resolved and downloaded for true offline installation without internet.
    
    * Skip tasksel software selection dialog
    
    Mark tasksel/first as already seen to prevent the interactive
    dialog from appearing, while still installing the pre-selected
    standard utilities and ssh-server.
    
    * Add verification of key packages in local repository
    
    After building the repository, verify that critical packages are present:
    - packetfence, packetfence-pfcmd-suid
    - docker.io, containerd
    - mariadb-server, redis-server
    - freeradius, fingerbank-collector
    
    Build fails if any key package is missing. Also shows package breakdown
    by category for debugging.
    
    * Add required packages for USB ISO build job
    
    * Run create-local-repo.sh with sudo for debootstrap
    
    debootstrap requires root privileges to create the chroot environment.
    Added chown after to restore file ownership to the CI runner user.
    
    * Run create-local-repo.sh in Docker container instead of sudo
    
    debootstrap requires root privileges, but sudo is not available in CI
    without a TTY. Run the script inside a debian:bookworm container where
    we have root access. This follows the same pattern as the regular
    debian-installer build.
    
    * Revert "Run create-local-repo.sh in Docker container instead of sudo"
    
    This reverts commit ffb1fec742ae267fdfd833e4c8236ce57afa2fbf.
    
    * Use sudo for individual commands instead of entire script
    
    Move sudo to specific commands that require root privileges:
    - debootstrap (creates chroot)
    - chroot (enters chroot)
    - tee/mkdir/cp for writing to chroot directories
    - rm for cleanup of chroot
    - chown to fix ownership after copying files
    
    This allows finer-grained sudoers configuration on the CI runner.
    
    * Skip tasksel software selection dialog in offline install
    
    Use pkgsel/run_tasksel=false to completely skip the interactive
    tasksel dialog when network is not configured. Add openssh-server
    to pkgsel/include since it was previously installed via tasksel.
    
    * Require root password during installation
    
    Disallow empty root password so the installer prompts the user
    to set a password during the installation process.
    
    * Enable CD-ROM as package source for base system packages
    
    The netinst ISO contains base Debian packages like systemd.
    Keep the CD-ROM enabled as a package source so the installer
    can find these packages during offline installation.
    
    * Remove CD-ROM apt source after installation instead of commenting
    
    Delete the cdrom line from sources.list rather than commenting it
    to prevent 'Please insert CD' prompts when running apt update.
    
    * Use tasksel with standard and ssh-server for USB ISO installation
    
    Match the regular ISO software selection by using tasksel instead of
    skipping it. This provides proper software selection options during
    installation (standard system utilities and SSH server) rather than
    only manually installing packages.
    
