    - Comment out 'grub-installer/bootdev string default' to prompt user
    - User will now be asked to select:
      1. Which disk to partition for installation
      2. Where to install the GRUB bootloader
    
    This fixes the issue where the system boots to a GRUB prompt after reboot.
    
    * usb-bootable-iso: Fix GRUB installation to show device selection menu
    
    The previous configuration was asking for manual /dev entry instead of
    showing a list of devices. This was caused by only_debian=true which
    tries to auto-detect but fails with multiple disks.
    
    Changes:
