    * usb-bootable-iso: Implement two-phase installation for Docker support
    
    The preseed late_command runs in a chroot environment where systemd
    is not running and Docker daemon cannot start. This caused PacketFence
    installation to fail because its postinst requires Docker.
    
    Solution: Split installation into two phases:
    
    Phase A (postinst-offline.sh - runs during preseed):
    - Configure APT repository from ISO
    - Install packages not on DVD-1 (lnav, cgroupfs-mount)
    - Install Docker packages (but don't start Docker)
    - Install PacketFence dependencies (mariadb, freeradius, etc.)
    - Copy Docker images to /var/cache/packetfence-docker-images/
    - Configure system (SSH, repositories)
    - Create first-boot service
    
    Phase B (packetfence-first-boot.sh - runs on first boot):
    - Start Docker service (now possible with systemd running)
    - Load Docker images from cache
    - Install PacketFence package (postinst can now use Docker)
    - Reset MariaDB root password
    - Cleanup (remove image cache, local repo config)
    - Start services
    
    🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
    
