    * usb-bootable-iso: Fix PacketFence installation without ISO mounted
    
    The first-boot script was failing at Step 3 because it tried to install
    PacketFence using apt-get, which required access to the local repository
    at /media/cdrom/pf-repo. However, the ISO/USB is removed after installation
    as instructed to the user.
    
    Solution:
    - Phase A (preseed): Copy packetfence_*.deb from ISO to /var/cache/packetfence-install/
    - Phase B (first boot): Install using dpkg -i from cached .deb file
    - Remove broken repository config before installation attempt
    - Clean up cached .deb after successful installation
    
    This allows PacketFence to install successfully without requiring the ISO
    to remain mounted.
    
