commit b89c751d7042f6af6c32a15917c481fbc9b18f78
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Apr 28 20:52:57 2026 -0400

    Roles: materialize parent_id from advanced.default_role_parent_id on create
    
    When a role is created via the API without a parent_id field,
    cleanupBeforeCommit now writes parent_id=<advanced.default_role_parent_id>
    into roles.conf (or parent_id= if the default is unset), instead of
    unconditionally writing an empty parent_id=. This pins the role's parent
    at creation time so a later change to advanced.default_role_parent_id
    cannot retroactively re-parent already-saved roles. On update, parent_id
    is never injected — existing roles keep whatever the user explicitly
    saved.
    
    The guard uses !defined (not !exists) because HTML::FormHandler's
    process(posted => 1) returns parent_id as undef rather than omitting the
    key when the API payload doesn't include it.

