commit 9e2e7912fa731aefe6f5e0d85f5e598e63825528
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Apr 28 09:11:44 2026 -0400

    Fix role ACL inheritance: don't materialize parent ACLs into child rows
    
    When a role was created with parent_id but no acls, pfconfig silently
    copied the parent's acls into the child via the generic-copy path,
    making include_parent_acls misleading. Now cleanupBeforeCommit defaults
    acls='' so the copy is skipped, and Switch.pm walks parent_id at runtime
    so nodes still receive the nearest ancestor's ACLs at radius/push-acl
    time without materialization into node_category.acls.

