    using virtualswitch MAB with device-specific DHCP fingerprints.
    
    * Add dot1x_wired_computer_auth_virtualswitch test suite
    
    Test 802.1X EAP-PEAP authentication using virtualswitch dot1x plug
    with local user credentials, verifying RADIUS audit log and VLAN
    assignment.
    
    * Add pfacct_bandwidth_virtualswitch test suite
    
    Test pfacct bandwidth accounting with virtualswitch, verifying RADIUS
    accounting data flows, bandwidth_accounting table population, and
    node online/offline/unregistered state transitions.
    
    * Add security_events_virtualswitch test suite
    
    Combined five security event scenarios into a single suite with phases:
    manual trigger (000), MAC detection (020), Fingerbank detection (050),
    delayed enforcement (080), and accounting/bandwidth trigger (110).
    Each phase tests a different trigger mechanism with isolation VLAN
    enforcement and event lifecycle.
    
    * Add vlan_inheritance_virtualswitch test suite
    
    Test VLAN inheritance across role hierarchy using virtualswitch. Verifies
    VLAN assignment follows inheritance chain through switch group roles,
    including fallback behavior when intermediate VLANs are removed or
    inheritance is disabled.
    
    * Update mac_auth_virtualswitch scenario to consolidated test suite
    
    The wired_mac_auth_virtualswitch and wireless_mac_auth_virtualswitch
    test suites were combined into a single mac_auth_virtualswitch suite in
    a0599db32e, but the scenario still referenced the old names.
    
    * Split security_events_virtualswitch back into 5 per-flow test suites
    
    Restore the per-flow structure that was consolidated in 312893ff57:
      - security_event_manual_virtualswitch
      - security_event_detect_mac_virtualswitch
      - security_event_detect_fingerbank_virtualswitch
      - security_event_delayed_virtualswitch
      - security_event_acct_virtualswitch
    
    The scenario at scenarios/security_event_virtualswitch/playbooks/run_tests.yml
    already references these 5 names, so it was broken against the consolidated
    directory. Splitting restores scenario/test_suite alignment.
    
    Content is restored from b934228e88 with 4 files ported forward from the
    consolidated version to preserve post-split improvements:
      - acct/02_restart_pfacct.yml + acct/teardown/12_restart_pfacct.yml:
        add stop + bandwidth_accounting cleanup + async restart
      - acct/16_wait_for_bandwidth_threshold.yml: replace fixed 45s sleep with
        MySQL polling loop
      - delayed/22_close_security_event.yml: add find_security_event search step
        so the close does not rely on cross-file variable passing
    
    Per-directory TESTSUITE.md and teardown/ are restored from the split state
    at b934228e88.
    
    * Port post-split improvements from consolidated security_events suite
    
    These 4 files were improved during the consolidation commit (312893ff57)
    that has since been reverted. Porting the improvements forward to the
    restored split suites so no work is lost:
    
    - security_event_acct_virtualswitch/02_restart_pfacct.yml and
      teardown/12_restart_pfacct.yml: add explicit pf_api_service_stop and
      bandwidth_accounting table cleanup before the restart, and switch to
      pf_api_service_restart_async.
    - security_event_acct_virtualswitch/16_wait_for_bandwidth_threshold.yml:
      replace the fixed 45s sleep with a MySQL polling loop that retries up
      to 15 times every 5s until the per-mac byte sum exceeds 500KB.
    - security_event_delayed_virtualswitch/22_close_security_event.yml: add
      a find_security_event search step before the close so the row id is
      looked up from the API rather than relying on cross-file variable
      passing from 18_check_security_event_open.yml.
    
    * Split mac_auth_virtualswitch back into wired and wireless suites
    
    Restore the per-flow structure that was consolidated in a0599db32e:
      - wired_mac_auth_virtualswitch (headless device MAB + printer/Fingerbank)
      - wireless_mac_auth_virtualswitch (wifi MAB on interface 7)
    
    The scenario at scenarios/mac_auth_virtualswitch/playbooks/run_tests.yml
    is reverted to referencing these two split names (undoing 4fdbfd0bb2),
    restoring the pre-consolidation wiring.
    
    Content is restored from b934228e88 with these improvements ported forward:
      - wired teardown/04_unplug_all_interfaces.yml: include interfaces 6-7
        (matches wireless teardown which was already correct)
      - wireless 07_clean_radius_audit_log.yml: reword title for clarity
      - New wired 04_enable_dns_recording_restart_services.yml: turn on
        record_dns_in_sql before the mac_auth flows so DNS audit log checks
        have data to match
      - Wireless teardown 46_restart_pfcron_service.yml is renamed to
        46_disable_dns_recording_restart_services.yml, turning DNS recording
        back off at the end of the scenario (this is the last suite to run)
        while still restarting pfcron async
    
    Per-directory TESTSUITE.md notes updated to mention the DNS recording
    enable/disable lifecycle.
    
    * Harden virtualswitch_api HTTP status check and add curl timeout
    
    Assert HTTP status via exact equality on the parsed code inside the
    script instead of ShouldContainSubstring on the full curl output, which
    could match the expected digits anywhere in the response body (e.g., a
    JSON field or error message containing "200"). Also pass --max-time so
    a stalled endpoint can't hang CI; failures now surface as a non-zero
    exit and trigger the existing retry/delay loop.
    
    * Actually assert printer VLAN assignment in 46_check_printer_vlan_assignment
    
    The step's name advertised a VLAN assignment check but only asserted the
    node's category/role, so the suite would pass even when the wrong VLAN
    was pushed to the port. Add a second testcase that queries the
    virtualswitch device status and asserts
    virtualswitch_device_status__vlan_assigned equals the configured printer
    role vlan_id (same pattern as the security_event_* and
    vlan_inheritance_* suites). Also fix the misleading "(200)" in the title
    — the configured printer VLAN is 2 per vars/all.yml — by templating the
    actual vlan_id into the name.
    
    * Use printer role variable instead of hard-coded value in fingerbank check
    
    Replace the literal "printer" string in 44_check_printer_fingerbank_detection
    with {{.wired_mac_auth_virtualswitch.roles.printer.id}}, matching the
    pattern used in 46_check_printer_vlan_assignment and every other place
    the role id is referenced. Keeps the test decoupled from the specific
    role name so renaming the role in vars/all.yml can't silently leave
    this step comparing against a stale string.
    
    * Fix 'overriden' typo in security_event_virtualswitch run_tests comment
    
    * Drop unused check_stop input from pf_api_check_radacct executor
    
    The input was declared with a default of "false" but never referenced
    in the SQL query, assertions, or var extractions — nothing in the body
    branches on it. Grep across the repo also shows zero callers of this
    executor, so no call site is passing the flag either. Removing it
    avoids confusing future callers who might assume it toggles a
    stop-time check. If stop-time verification is ever needed, it can be
    reintroduced alongside the concrete caller that requires it.
    
    * Assert configreload hard success in security_event_detect_mac create step
    
    The exec step running `pfcmd configreload hard` had no assertions, so a
    failed reload (missing binary, permission error, config parse failure)
    would silently pass and the real symptom would only surface later as a
    Fingerbank / VLAN mismatch in the downstream detection steps. Add
    `result.code ShouldEqual 0` to make the failure surface at the step
    that actually produced it.
    
    * Gate DNS audit flush on Redis state to avoid empty-flush race
    
    The wired virtualswitch DNS audit check could flush an empty list and
    the downstream search would 404 on a fresh DB (the suite lost its
    previous service-restart warmup, so the simulated device's first DNS
    queries can land after the flush fires). Poll `LLEN DNS_AUDIT_LOG > 0`
    (up to 60s) inside the `pfcron_flush_dns_audit_log` lib executor before
    running the flush so it only proceeds once pfdns has buffered at least
    one entry.
    
    * Restore service restart step in wired_mac_auth_virtualswitch as 05
    
    Commit 238932022b removed `04_restart_services.yml` on the assumption
    that the global_config_virtualswitch restart was sufficient. In
    practice the wired DNS audit check is now flaky on EL8 — restoring
    the seven-service restart (35s of warmup) brings wired in line with
    the wireless suite, which still has the equivalent step and passes
    reliably.
    
    Renumbered to `05_` so it runs after `04_enable_dns_recording_restart_services.yml`
    and before `06_enable_node_cleanup_task.yml`, fitting the existing
    numbering gap.
    
    * Revert "Gate DNS audit flush on Redis state to avoid empty-flush race"
    
    This reverts commit 4c880c4ef14a48fcdde41d297553bd93adca0a42.

