commit a5b0180ef8e173eabe02c9c7101f0abf464b5aff
Author: Satkunas <3904468+satkunas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Apr 21 17:02:46 2026 -0400

    Added documentation and code to test if a account (User or Machine) has (#8971)
    
    * Added documentation and code to test if a account (User or Machine) has
    been disabled in the AD
    
    * Update FreeRADIUS version
    
    * Apply suggestion from @Copilot
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Escape LDAP username in _makefilter and test bitwise filter operators
    
    Apply escape_filter_value once inside _makefilter (including the
    {username} substitution in append_to_searchattributes) so all callers
    are safe by construction; drop the pre-escape in authenticate to
    avoid double-escaping. Add t/ldap-auth-filter-bitwise.t asserting the
    exact filter output for the 'has bit' and 'not has bit' operators,
    covering parenthesis grouping and negation placement.
    
    * Fix disabled-account rule example to reject instead of filter
    
    The previous example used `not has bit 2` as the rule condition, which
    matches enabled accounts. To actually reject disabled accounts, the
    condition must be `has bit 2` with the rule action set to role=REJECT
    and an access duration.
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
    Co-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

