commit c3db52f773b2691c998643a60d262729aa7a2f1d
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Apr 17 09:03:19 2026 -0400

    Pin clean-css-cli for docs build to avoid interactive npx prompt
    
    The Makefile rule that minifies docs/styles/app.css invoked
    `npx --package clean-css-cli cleancss ...` without --yes, so each
    fresh environment (CI, Docker layers, new dev boxes) was blocked by
    an interactive "Ok to proceed?" prompt.
    
    Pin clean-css-cli@5.6.3 in a new docs/package.json, install it once
    into docs/node_modules when package.json changes, and call the local
    binary directly. Also extend `make clean` to remove docs/node_modules.

M	Makefile
A	docs/package.json

commit e67d8cca6c76c3d7668f4ae15e802eaebb4cdfae
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Apr 17 08:27:03 2026 -0400

    Fix switch edit page performance with many roles
    
    The switch editing page was extremely slow with 1000+ roles due to:
    - O(n²) object spreads in the store and schema when pre-declaring role mappings
    - All roles rendered simultaneously in the DOM (up to 8800 components)
    - Hardcoded limit of 1000 in the roles API request
    - O(n×m) linear scans in backend metadata generation
    
    Changes:
    - Replace O(n²) object spreads with single-pass O(n) property assignment
    - Add virtual scrolling (BaseRoleMapList) to render only visible roles
    - Add search/filter input on the Roles tab to quickly find roles
    - Increase roles API limit from 1000 to 9999
    - Use hash lookups instead of linear scans in backend cleanup_options
    - Apply same fixes to switchGroups form

