commit 064ae420fe6fa0662e6bcb6ead5f63c117ff3111
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 6 16:30:45 2026 -0400

    Use cached db_check_readonly() to avoid ProxySQL write-hostgroup timeout
    
    db_readonly_mode() runs SELECT @@global.read_only which ProxySQL routes
    to hostgroup 10 (writer). During Galera failover with no writable backend,
    this query times out for ~10s blocking admin login. Switch to
    db_check_readonly() which caches the result for 5s via CHI, avoiding
    repeated queries to the dead hostgroup.

M	lib/pf/UnifiedApi/Controller.pm

commit 2c20460a41745fc3f7edcadc4dcf47ae18d612e8
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 6 14:23:52 2026 -0400

    Skip audit logging when database is in read-only mode
    
    When the DB is read-only (e.g. Galera failover), the audit INSERT
    routes to ProxySQL hostgroup 10 which has no writable backend,
    causing a 10s timeout that blocks admin login. Check db_readonly_mode()
    in is_auditable() to skip the write entirely.

