commit b35f3226d17e0dd6ca269e958a72dcd983ef924a
Author: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>
Date:   Tue Jan 13 17:06:25 2026 +0000

      Add URL query parameter autofill for captive portal forms
    
      Add generic JavaScript solution to pre-populate form fields from URL
      query parameters (e.g., ?username=foo, ?identifier=bar, ?email=x@y.com).
    
      Changes:
      - Add initQueryParams() function to captiveportal.js that:
        - Parses URL query parameters on page load
        - Fills visible input fields matching parameter names (by name or id)
        - Skips hidden fields and preserves existing values
        - Uses MutationObserver to re-trigger autofill when cards become
          visible during multi-step workflows (e.g., after AUP acceptance)
      - Pass username to password reset success template so the Login link
        includes ?username= parameter for seamless login after reset
    
      This enables external systems to link to captive portal pages with
      pre-filled user information, improving the user experience.

