commit ffec1eea67720bf72d5d846ecc88984d186ec8b2
Author: dsatkunas <dsatkuna@akamai.com>
Date:   Thu Jan 8 19:00:41 2026 +0000

    Add unauthenticated password recovery to captive portal
    
      Implement password reset functionality for the captive portal that allows
      users to reset their password via email without being logged in.
    
      Features:
      - Forgot password form accessible from login page (/status/forgot_password)
      - Email-based password reset with secure token (1-hour expiration)
      - Rate limiting: 3 requests per hour per user via pf::rate_limiter
      - Generic responses to prevent user enumeration attacks
      - Token validation and password reset flow (/status/reset_password_token)
    
      Implementation uses existing activation table infrastructure with new
      'password_reset' type, following established patterns for guest/sponsor
      activation flows. No database schema changes required.
    
      Files modified:
      - lib/pf/activation.pm: Add PASSWORD_RESET_ACTIVATION constant and
        create_and_send_password_reset() function
      - lib/pf/password.pm: Add initiate_password_reset() and
        reset_password_with_token() functions
      - html/captive-portal/lib/captiveportal/PacketFence/Controller/Status.pm:
        Add forgot_password and reset_password_token routes
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/login.html: Add forgot password link
    
      Files created:
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/forgot_password.html
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/forgot_password_sent.html
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/reset_password_token.html
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/reset_password_token_invalid.html
      - html/captive-portal/templates/status/reset_password_token_success.html
      - html/captive-portal/templates/emails/emails-guest_password_reset.html

