commit 43a47b52a1232ae312d2326583dc7d27f822244e
Author: JeGoi <13801368+JeGoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Dec 12 10:01:54 2025 -0500

    fix(ci): use shell-based TEST_ONLY filtering instead of rules
    
    GitLab CI doesn't expand variables inside regex patterns in rules,
    so `$CI_JOB_NAME !~ $TEST_ONLY` was doing literal string comparison.
    Move the TEST_ONLY check to .test_script_job using shell grep -E,
    which properly supports variable expansion in regex patterns.
    
    Jobs that don't match TEST_ONLY will now exit immediately with a
    "Skipping" message instead of being filtered out at the rules level.
    
    🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

M	.gitlab-ci.yml

