commit 4ef2c165c7c945d0f2781928b3a37c6444db904d
Author: JeGoi <13801368+JeGoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Dec 11 08:59:41 2025 -0500

    feat(ci): add selective test execution via TEST_ONLY variable
    
    Implement TEST_ONLY variable to allow running specific test jobs
    instead of all tests when TEST=yes is set.
    
    Changes:
    - Add TEST_ONLY variable to gitlab-ci.yml variables section
    - Update .test_devel_and_maintenance_rules to filter by TEST_ONLY
    - Update .test_branches_only_rules to filter by TEST_ONLY
    
    Usage examples:
      TEST=yes TEST_ONLY=mac_auth           # Run only mac_auth tests
      TEST=yes TEST_ONLY=configurator|unit  # Run multiple tests
      TEST=yes TEST_ONLY=_deb12             # Run only Debian 12 tests
    
    When TEST_ONLY is empty, all tests run (default behavior).

