commit 96de7722d76df02758ccf93f4ad5b04f0dc8760e
Author: Durand Fabrice <oeufdure@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Dec 1 12:48:07 2025 -0500

      Fix pfflow job hanging when Kafka is unresponsive during startup
    
      Two issues were identified and fixed:
    
      1. In kafka_submitter.go: Replace sync.Once with mutex-based retry
         mechanism. sync.Once is consumed even if the setup function panics
         or fails, preventing subsequent retry attempts within the same
         process. Now uses a mutex + boolean flag that only marks success
         after everything is properly initialized. Also adds retry loop for
         database connection instead of panicking.
    
      2. In pfflowjob.go: Add 60-second timeout to ReadMessage() call.
         Previously used context.Background() which never times out. If Kafka
         accepts the TCP connection but doesn't respond (e.g., during Kafka
         startup), ReadMessage() would block forever. The job appeared to be
         running (showing "Skipped pfflow") but was actually stuck, not
         processing any messages. Timeout errors are handled separately from
         connection errors - timeouts just retry immediately while connection
         errors trigger exponential backoff reconnection.

M	go/cron/kafka_submitter.go
M	go/cron/pfflowjob.go

